  "body": "Report template patching in mutation records\n\nPass an active template and status to DOM's insert and remove algorithms (and queue a tree mutation record) for parser mutations done on behalf of a `template` element with a `for` attribute, so that mutation observers that opt in using `activeTemplateAttributeFilter` can tell when a patch starts, is updated, ends, or is aborted.\n\nRemoving the start marker and fallback content now happens as a single \"`start`\" record when patching begins; removing the end marker at `</template>` is the \"`end`\" record. A missing target, end-of-file before `</template>`, and aborting the parser report \"`abort`\".\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64641.\n\nFixes #13008.\n\n---\n\nThis depends on whatwg/dom#1518, which adds the `MutationObserverInit` and `MutationRecord` members and the new insert/remove/queue a tree mutation record parameters. The two PRs need to land together.\n\nI drafted this PR, the DOM PR, and the tests with an AI coding agent (Gemini in Antigravity), based on the proposed design in #13008 and the [explainer](https://github.com/WICG/declarative-partial-updates/blob/main/template-mutation-observer-explainer.md). I made the judgement calls: following the explainer for start/end timing (which drops the \"insertion start marker\" state and changes when `<?start>` is removed compared to `main`), implying `childList`, and the scope of \"`abort`\".\n\nOut of scope, as possible follow-ups:\n* A marker that is moved or removed by script mid-stream\n* A container that is detached mid-stream\n* `<template for src>`\n* Character data updates, including the parser appending text to an existing `Text` node (#12744)\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64641\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13181/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 3, 2026, 11:42 AM UTC (ce9e0be)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13181/404b3eb...ce9e0be/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 3, 2026, 11:42 AM UTC (ce9e0be)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13181/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 3, 2026, 11:42 AM UTC (ce9e0be)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13181/404b3eb...ce9e0be/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 3, 2026, 11:42 AM UTC (ce9e0be)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13181/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 3, 2026, 11:42 AM UTC (ce9e0be)\">/scripting.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13181/404b3eb...ce9e0be/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 3, 2026, 11:42 AM UTC (ce9e0be)\">diff</a> )",
